#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-SEND-0277 expect=noViolation domain=BW
#note "The negative half of the 'uri=' contract, and the probe that proves the attribute is load-bearing: identical to the invalid twin except that no uri= is declared, so getTableURI() is null, $dataset_location is null, the regex folds a missing value to the empty string and nothing fires. Matches the withUri(null) arm of Cx1FileMetadataRulesProbeTest.send277_firesOnUppercaseFileName. The verdict is noViolation, not skipped: extract_metadata needs no provider, so the rule executes either way."
#library standard=sendig version=3-1-1
#expectViolationCount 0
dataset BW class=FINDINGS label="Body Weight"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID  type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col BWSEQ    type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col BWTESTCD type=Char label="Test Short Name"
col BWORRES  type=Char label="Result or Findings as Collected"
---
S1 | BW | 001 | 1 | BW | 250
S1 | BW | 002 | 1 | BW | 260
